I first started reading Hack and Nethack code in the 1980s before the
ANSI-c standard and before the object oriented movement.  For its size
and age Nethack is very good code.  This is a perspective lost in time -
Think of it in terms of Moore's Law.  The Nethack binaries still fits on
a floppy because floppies were the common technology then.  A machine
with a megabyte of RAM was a good sized machine.  I saw my first
gigabyte disk drive only a couple of years before I read my first
Nethack code - The drive was the size of a coin-op laundry machine.

Development technology has changed much slower than hardware, but the
code is now 3 *decades* old.

